  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/51020439-088d-4dd9-9753-1be19f84c709.png\" style=\"max-width:\"100%\"; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:2.13333in;height:1.8in\" /></p><p>Circle touches the&nbsp;<math><mi>x</mi></math> -axis at <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />So, center of circle is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and radius is <math><mi>k</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br />Hence, the equation of circle is:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br />It passes through the point <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> ,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math><mo>∴</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
